    "final_answer": "I have successfully identified the storage options for the latest iPad Pro on the Apple website.\n\n## Available Storage Options for the Latest iPad Pro\n\nThe latest iPad Pro (powered by the M5 chip) is available in **four storage configurations**, applicable to both the 11-inch and 13-inch models:\n\n| Storage | Memory | Chip Configuration | Starting Price (11\") | Starting Price (13\") |\n|---------|--------|-------------------|---------------------|---------------------|\n| **256GB** | 12GB | M5 (9-core CPU, 10-core GPU) | $1,199 | $1,499 |\n| **512GB** | 12GB | M5 (9-core CPU, 10-core GPU) | $1,399 | $1,699 (est.) |\n| **1TB** | 16GB | M5 (10-core CPU, 10-core GPU) | $1,799 | $2,099 (est.) |\n| **2TB** | 16GB | M5 (10-core CPU, 10-core GPU) | $2,299 | $2,599 (est.) |\n\n### Key observations:\n- **256GB and 512GB** models come with 12GB unified memory and an M5 chip with 9-core CPU / 10-core GPU.\n- **1TB and 2TB** models include 16GB unified memory and an upgraded M5 chip with 10-core CPU / 10-core GPU.\n- Storage is offered across **two display sizes**: 11-inch (starting at $1,199) and 13-inch (starting at $1,499).\n- All configurations are available in the \"Buy iPad Pro\" configurator on apple.com.\n\nThese four storage tiers are clearly displayed in the \"Storage, memory, and chip. Choose your configuration.\" section of the iPad Pro purchase page.",
